PAGE TUNER
TITLE The antenna tuner
KIND topic
SCREENS TUNER
SEE FORM-CHANNEL EMCON
BEGIN_TEXT
The LDG tuner has two antenna ports, 1 and 2. Each channel names one port
to listen on (RX antenna) and one to transmit on (TX antenna), on the
CHANNEL form. A channel that names none uses port 1 for both. Use one port
for both, or receive on a quiet antenna and transmit on the other.

The tuner never switches with RF on. On a channel change it moves to the
channel's RX port and recalls that channel's tuner memory. Before each
transmit, with RF off, it moves to the TX port; the radio keys only once
the tuner says it is there. After the transmit, once the radio is unkeyed
and the keying program has stopped, it moves back to the RX port. If it
can't, the receiver may still be on the TX antenna: the log says so.

A tune keys a steady carrier of 25 W or less on the TX port, tunes, and
stores the result in that channel's memory. The box holds the 25 W limit
itself, and the tuner refuses more. A tune needs your Y each time.

While transmit is pinned to recorded files, as it is today, a tune is
refused: a tune is a transmit. EMCON refuses it too.

Keying is by CAT or the radio's PTT line only. VOX is never used.

With no tuner connected, the box sends as it would without one.
END
